                        "review": "I've only had this game for a short while, but it's turned out to be everything I'd hoped for. Anyone who has played the dubiously named \"Skidmarks\" on the Amiga will know what to expect. The physics are very dodgy indeed - as they should be in this type of game - and under my control the poor cars go flying off in all directions. So far I've had around five races on the easy level and have come last in every one of them - but that's because I'm useless at this type of game and not the game's fault!\nI'm sure there are people around who would be able to ramp up the difficulty level and still win every time - but personally, I'm still having fun rolling my vehicle all over the place and coming last.\nRight - I'm going to stop writing, switch the difficulty level down to \"very easy\" and have another go. In the meantime, do yourself a nostalgic favour and click \"Buy Now\"!!!",
